notes: "Autosave keeps your work, but some moments deserve a name: figures final, sent to co-authors, lab meeting version. In History you type a name and save a slide version. It keeps the slide, its Story and the exact images it used, and it lives inside the project folder, so it moves with the project. This capture shows slide N014 with two named versions; the older one, Before copy edit, is selected and previewed read-only, with the original title. The Operation history tab lists every saved operation with its review. Restoring a version changes only that slide. That matters for science talks: you can roll back one figure without disturbing the rest of the deck, and a Presentation can pin a named version where it must not change."
